      "_layoutInvariant": "VERTICAL IS STRICTLY SEQUENTIAL — at no instant may two (phase,anchor) groups both be on screen. Windows incl. exit fade: hook|upperThird 0.2-2.45, proof|upperThird 2.67-5.10, close|lowerThird 5.12-end. WHY: Canonical.jsx resolveGroupAnchor shifts each group off a face/product band INDEPENDENTLY, with no knowledge of where other groups landed, and stackContainerStyle then positions purely from the resolved anchor — so two simultaneous groups whose keep-out chains converge paint on top of each other. Overlapping windows were the cause of the delivered text-on-text defect on ads 6a93ade2e4f1d02784398630 / 6a93ade1e4f1d02784398626 (2026-08-30), where the close stack (then authored in `hook` from 1.5s with no exit) was pushed onto upperThird through the live headline. Pinned by scripts/verifyTitleGroupsNeverOverlap.js — if you re-time this preset and that harness goes red, the collision is back; do not relax it."
    },
